          model: "The matching (accruals) concept requires the statement of profit or loss to show the expenses incurred in earning the year's income, not the cash paid. Wages for the last week of the year were used to earn this year's sales, so they belong in this year's expenses even if they are paid next year. If the $800 accrual were omitted, wages would be understated by $800, so profit for the year would be overstated by $800. In the statement of financial position, current liabilities (other payables) would be understated by $800 and capital would be overstated by $800.",
          points: ["Matching or accruals concept named (1)", "Expenses incurred in the year must be charged whatever the payment date (1)", "Omission: expenses understated and profit overstated by $800 (1)", "Omission: current liabilities understated and capital overstated by $800 (1)"],
