          prompt: "At 31 December 2026 Rana held 120 units of product P, which cost $15 each and have a net realisable value of $14 each, and 50 units of product Q, which cost $22 each and have a net realisable value of $30 each. Calculate the value of closing inventory.",
          model: "Product P: NRV $14 is lower than cost $15, so 120 x $14 = $1,680. Product Q: cost $22 is lower than NRV $30, so 50 x $22 = $1,100. Closing inventory = $1,680 + $1,100 = $2,780.",
          points: ["P valued at $14 per unit (1)", "P total $1,680 (1)", "Q valued at cost, $1,100 (1)", "Closing inventory $2,780 (1)"],
